cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "commensurability: diagnostics for cell-type label commensurability in spatial omics"
version: 1.0.0
type: software
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-19"
abstract: >-
  Diagnostics for testing whether two cell-type labels can legitimately be
  compared, and for measuring how much a spatial conclusion depends on the
  definitions used to produce it. Provides three diagnostic layers (label, effect,
  platform), a sensitivity summary, a reporting audit against a minimal reporting
  set, and self-contained synthetic demonstrations including a valid null
  construction. Ships with a test suite and needs no primary data download.
repository-code: "https://github.com/shenwen0212/commensurability"
url: "https://github.com/shenwen0212/commensurability"
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - cell-type annotation
  - reproducibility
  - commensurability
  - neighbourhood analysis
  - reporting standards
  - R
authors:
  - given-names: "Wen"
    family-names: "Shen"
    affiliation: "the Affiliated Huai'an Hospital of Xuzhou Medical University, the Second People's Hospital of Huai'an, Huai'an, Jiangsu 223002, China"
  # Add further authors here, in manuscript order, in the same form.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Cell-type labels are not interchangeable measurements: definition alignment
      decides the sign of spatial neighbourhood effects
    status: in-preparation
